Third-party components
----------------------
The local test suite uses a small number of .nbs fixtures from permissively
licensed open-source projects in order to verify the decoder against known-good
input. Those fixtures are NOT distributed with this repository, but the
attributions are retained here because the project depends on them during
development, and because anyone who obtains the test suite separately should see
where its input came from.

1. pynbs - https://github.com/OpenNBS/pynbs
   Copyright (c) Open Note Block Studio contributors
   Licensed under the MIT License.
   Used for: .nbs test fixtures and their parsed-output golden snapshots, as
   well as the minimal legacy/current song goldens.

2. nbs.js - https://github.com/OpenNBS/nbs.js
   Copyright (c) Open Note Block Studio contributors
   Licensed under the MIT License.
   Used for: the version 6 test fixture and its documented expected values.

3. Open Note Block Studio - https://github.com/OpenNBS/NoteBlockStudio
   Copyright (c) Open Note Block Studio contributors
   Licensed under the MIT License.
   Used for: the upstream demo songs that the above fixtures are derived from.

The distributed player itself contains NO third-party code: `nbs/`, `player/`,
`ccnbs.lua`, `ccnbsplayer.lua`, `installer.lua` and `qa/` are written from
scratch for this project.


